<div class="page-title"><h1>Materials</h1></div>
<div class="prose">

<p>The Microplotter employs ultrasonic liquid dispensing technology, enabling printing of a wide range of ink types &mdash; those compatible with standard inkjet printers, plus additional formulations. The system supports inks with viscosities from 0 centipoise up to 450 centipoise, and suspensions with particles ranging from nanometers up to 15 microns in size. Both aqueous solutions and organic solvent-based inks work well with the technology.</p>

<h2>Ink partners</h2>

<h3>Sigma-Aldrich</h3>
<p>Supplies organic and nanoparticle inks, polymers, and graphene for bioelectronics and sensor applications.</p>

<h3>Xerox</h3>
<p>Offers silver nanoparticle ink, dielectrics, organic semiconductor, and nanotube solutions.</p>

<h3>Applied Nanotech</h3>
<p>Provides high-performance, cost-effective nanoparticle inks for printed electronics.</p>

<h3>Promethean Particles</h3>
<p>Operates a large-scale nanomaterials production facility specializing in conductive nano-copper and nano-silver dispersions.</p>

<h3>Cabot</h3>
<p>Manufactures electrically conductive polymers, composites, and battery electrode inks.</p>

<h3>Creative Materials</h3>
<p>Develops adhesives, coatings, and both standard and custom ink formulations.</p>

<h3>DuPont</h3>
<p>Produces specialized inks for photovoltaic, automotive, biomedical, military, and consumer applications.</p>

<h3>InkTec</h3>
<p>Develops silver conductive inks using nano-particle chemistry.</p>

<h3>Johnson Matthey</h3>
<p>Supplies silver products and electrically conductive coatings globally.</p>

<h3>Novacentrix</h3>
<p>Offers Metalon&reg; conductive inks for photovoltaic devices, RFID, and advanced packaging.</p>

<h3>UT Dots</h3>
<p>Manufactures conductive silver, gold, and platinum nanoparticles for printed electronics.</p>

</div>
